WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:05.330
Halloween is coming, and while the big horror
releases have been teasing us for months,

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:09.110
August saw a wave of trailers for low-profile
horror movies that haven't yet caught the

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:09.920
public eye.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:15.740
From a psychotic RV to sadistic dance instructors
to a haunted pizza parlor, fear is going to

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.240
come in all flavors this year.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.240
Even if you aren't a horror fan, you'll find
a lot of other types of films to get excited

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:25.609
about in the coming months, so here's a roundup
of all the new movie trailers from August

00:00:25.609 --> 00:00:26.680
that'll blow you away.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.700
The Toybox

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.219
Combining the isolated desert setting of The
Hills Have Eyes with the innate horror of

00:00:33.219 --> 00:00:37.570
a family road trip, The Toybox is a movie
that asks the all-important question: What

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.300
if your RV was evil?

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.400
"Everything in this camper's going to die."

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:43.360
Silly?

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:43.860
Sure.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.440
But it's also the perfect horror villain.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.820
What are you going to do run away from it?

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:48.560
It's a car.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:49.140
It'll catch you.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:53.239
And when you're alone in the desert with nobody
around for miles, anything with wheels is

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:55.140
guaranteed to have the last laugh.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.560
Denise Richards and Mischa Barton headline
The Toybox, which revs into theaters on September

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.080
18th.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.960
Await Further Instructions

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.159
There are disastrous family reunions, and
then there's whatever's happening in the trailer

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:13.290
for Await Further Instructions, a sci-fi horror
film about a family that wakes up to find

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:16.660
all their windows and doors blocked by a strange
black shield.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:21.079
Their only clue about what's going on is a
sinister message on the TV telling them to

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.400
await further instructions.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.159
From indie production label Dark Sky Films,
the company behind recent genre films such

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:32.549
as Mohawk, It Stains the Sands Red, and the
masterpiece Birdemic, Await Further Instructions

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:37.070
looks like that rare low-budget film that
uses every last dollar to deliver a sleek,

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:38.070
stylish experience.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:41.080
You can take a look when it hits theaters
in early October.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.380
Bad Times at the El Royale

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:48.060
August's stylish trailer for Bad Times at
the El Royale does a great job of building

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:51.299
the excitement for what looks like one of
the best movies of the year.

00:01:51.299 --> 00:01:55.870
The trailer introduces the main characters
and offers a few tantalizing glimpses of the

00:01:55.870 --> 00:02:00.810
madness going down at the El Royale, a seedy
hotel on the border of Nevada and California

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:03.700
where the fates of seven strangers will come
to a head.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:08.880
Writer and director Drew Goddard took on his
first feature film in 2012 with Cabin in the

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:12.300
Woods, and this has the looks of yet another
genre classic in the making.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:17.060
Get ready for good times at the theater when
Bad Times at the El Royale checks in on October

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:17.580
12th.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:19.520
First Man

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:24.780
There's a lot of talent pouring into Universal's
upcoming historical drama First Man.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:29.700
Written by Josh Singer of Spotlight, directed
by Damien Chazelle of La-La Land, and produced

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:34.780
by Steven Spielberg, First Man tells the riveting
story of Apollo 11, the mission which saw

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:38.510
Neil Armstrong become the first man to set
foot on the lunar surface.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:43.230
Ryan Gosling steps into the space boots as
Armstrong, leading an amazing cast that includes

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:45.140
Claire Foy and Corey Stoll.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:49.380
The film will focus on the years leading up
to the historic moon landing and how the mounting

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.880
pressure took a toll on Armstrong's family
life.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:55.080
Check it out when First Man lands in theaters
on October 12th.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:57.100
Air Strike

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.420
You'll get at least one chance to take a break
from the all horror in late October with Air

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:05.950
Strike, a World War II action thriller starring
Adrien Brody and Bruce Willis.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:11.230
Based on the true story of the Japanese bombing
of a Chinese town in 1941, Air Strike isn't

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:16.140
afraid to take that momentous historical tragedy
and turn it into a CGI action fest.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.760
"Sir, please allow us to go kick some ass"

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:23.040
So yeah, Air Strike doesn't look like it's
on track to win any awards, but there are

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.660
probably enough explosions here to make for
a fun time at the movies.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:29.040
Look for it in theaters on October 26th

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.040
Suspiria

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:35.360
Out of all the horror movies hitting theaters
this fall, who knew that the one about a ballet

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.320
school would look like one of the scariest?

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:42.020
And yet that seems to be the case with Suspiria,
an upcoming horror thriller produced by Amazon

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:42.520
Studios.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:48.160
This remake of the classic 1977 film takes
place at a dance academy where a new student

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:52.010
begins to suspect that something sinister
is going on behind the curtains.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:56.650
Judging by the trailer, Suspiria is banking
on a steep dive into psychological terror

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.150
and plenty of supernatural imagery to deliver
the chills.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:03.100
Take a look when it hits select theaters on
October 26th.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.140
A Private War

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.500
Based on a true story, A Private War chronicles
the life of foreign correspondent Marie Colvin,

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:15.210
who spent most of her career covering armed
conflicts around the world one of which ultimately

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:15.900
took her life.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:20.760
Rosamund Pike stars as Colvin, with Jamie
Dornan and Stanley Tucci co-starring.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:25.260
Expect plenty of hard-hitting drama when A
Private War hits theaters in limited release

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:29.240
on November 2nd, followed by a widespread
release on November 16th.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:31.120
Outlaw King

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:35.780
Most people probably know Robert the Bruce
as the guy in the chainmail hoodie who betrayed

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:40.100
William Wallace in Braveheart, but there's
a lot more to this Scottish hero than handsome

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.259
goatees and internal conflict.

00:04:42.259 --> 00:04:47.030
Netflix's upcoming Outlaw King follows Robert
on his bloody path from enemy of the crown

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:51.000
to King of Scots and his war against England
for Scottish independence.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.360
Chris Pine stars as Robert the Bruce, and
by the looks of the trailer, Outlaw King will

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:58.580
favor historical accuracy over fictionalized
drama.

00:04:58.789 --> 00:05:02.760
Outlaw King will enjoy a limited theatrical
release on November 9th before streaming on

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:03.260
Netflix.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:05.340
Slice

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:10.840
No doubt about it 2018 is a serious year for
serious horror movies, which is why a good

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:14.040
horror comedy like Slice is such a welcome
change of pace.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.080
This A24 production centers on a pizza place
that also happens to be a gateway to hell,

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.320
and a werewolf that's picking off the delivery
staff.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:26.139
It's up to Astrid, played by Zazie Beetz,
to track down the werewolf and stop the legions

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:27.800
of hell from taking over the town.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.600
"Looks like I'm going on a wolf hunt tonight."

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.600
Slice is set to be released in Fall 2018.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:34.680
Heretiks

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:37.440
Nuns are the perfect vehicle for horror.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:41.949
With their suspicious black-and-white habits
and their easy access to creepy church basements,

00:05:41.949 --> 00:05:45.120
nuns and terror are the cinematic peanut butter
and jelly.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.780
You don't even have to try, and you still
get a good sandwich.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:52.120
And Heretiks is delivering the goods with
a nun-based creepfest straight out of your

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:52.620
nightmares.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:55.900
This movie has nuns in all the shadows, and
shadows in every corner.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:06:00.740
Is it a little convenient that Heretiks is
coming out right alongside Warner Bros.' high-profile

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:02.080
chapel chiller The Nun?

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:06.060
Probably, but it still looks like it'll hit
all the right notes for a fun, late-night

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:06.560
horror flick.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:11.360
Heretiks still doesn't have a specific release
date, so fingers crossed it doesn't...sneak

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:11.980
up on us.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.220
Check it out sometime in 2018.

